From b166305b7a4ec0d567b14c5d623f7ffc6876aed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:13:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Translate llvm.minimum/maximum with NaN-propagating semantics
 (#4032)

Fixes #3282: `llvm.minimum`/`llvm.maximum` were translated to OpenCL.std
`fmin`/`fmax`, which ignore NaN operands. They also don't order -0.0
before +0.0, which `llvm.minimum`/`llvm.maximum` require.

Assisted by: Opus 5.5
